1	The beginning	The morning arrived without ceremony, as mornings often do, carrying with it the quiet weight of things that had already been decided. Light filtered through the window in a way that suggested time was moving forward regardless of intention, habit, or resistance. There was nothing remarkable about the room, yet it felt dense with the residue of past thoughts, half-finished plans, and moments postponed for later. Somewhere between waking and remembering, the day had already begun asking its first, unspoken questions.\n\nOutside, the world went on with its familiar indifference. People moved, objects changed hands, conversations started and ended without leaving a trace. Inside, however, everything felt slower, as if meaning needed permission to emerge. It was in this gap — between action and reflection, noise and silence — that something like a beginning waited, patient and undefined, ready to be noticed or ignored.	1	2026-02-10 07:42:48.590829+01	2026-02-10 15:38:33.161761+01	1
